    "body": "## Overview\n\nPreserve fractional Prometheus counter values in `get_metrics_snapshot()`. The current integer conversion truncates duration counters such as KV offload load and store times, making a value of 0.125 seconds appear as zero through the metrics reader.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Return the original counter sample value and describe `Counter.value` as a float.\n- Keep the special speculative token vector conversion unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nOn DGX Spark with the current source and an existing Python environment:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python -m pytest --confcutdir=tests/v1/metrics tests/v1/metrics/test_metrics_reader.py -q\n```\n\n12 tests pass. Against the original reader, the four fractional counter cases fail and eight existing/control cases pass. The cases use real Prometheus counters with one and four engine label sets. All applicable pre-commit hooks pass.\n\nThe test command isolates the CPU metrics suite from the model test fixtures in the root conftest. No model evaluation was run: the change reads telemetry and does not modify model execution or generated output.\n\n## Details\n\nKV offload metrics already accumulate floating point transfer durations. Converting their samples to `int` silently discards information. Preserve the value as exported by Prometheus; integral counts remain numerically equal, but callers inspecting the Python type will now see a float.\n\nDuplicate checks searched open PRs and issues for counter fractional values, counter truncation, and fractional metrics. No matching fix was found. This is separate from #46920, which handles unsupported metric types.\n\nAI assistance: implemented, reviewed, and tested with Codex. Human review is pending.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull Request Checklist</summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Preserves the Prometheus value without changing collection or engine code.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Real counter regression covers fractional and integral values, with baseline failures verified.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Reuses the existing test and updates the public dataclass description.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes behavior, duplicate checks, test results, and compatibility details.\n</details>\n",
